ASSISTANT Summary of the changes:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 1. **Replaced the `fileSystems."/run/agent-keys"` entry with an explicit `systemd.mounts` unit** — a `what = "devtools-config"` / `type = "9p"` / `options = "trans=virtio,version=9p2000.L,ro"` mount at `/run/agent-keys`, pulled in at boot via `wantedBy = [ "multi-user.target" ]`. This generates the unit directly (unit name: `run-run-agent-keys.mount`), bypassing the fstab generator.
ASSISTANT 2. **Made the agent service depend on the mount** — `requires` + `after` on `run-run-agent-keys.mount`, so the agent only starts once the 9p share is mounted, and fails (rather than running keyless) if the mount fails.
ASSISTANT 3. Kept `boot.initrd.availableKernelModules` / `boot.kernelModules` with `9p`/`9pnet_virtio` so the modules are loaded before systemd attempts the mount.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT I deliberately preserved your recent edits (the commented-out `graphics`/`kernelParams`, the journald console forwarding, the commented `StandardOutput = "kmsg"`, and the commented `OnFailure`).
